resolution": []}, "title": "I am a J6er. Had even one officer said, \u201cDo not go in,\u201d I would not have gone in. Had I seen one sign \u2014 one message from the largest PA system in the world telling us to stay out \u2014 I would not have gone in.", "last_comment_created": 1790436296475, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 19, "score_up": 449, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 3068, "created": 1790272697000, "id": "2103182248296259961", "video": {"preview": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2103182168881250304/img/v2F_0JmNqCAlqEKp.jpg", "mpeg": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2103182168881250304/pl/XYyexgyhoxvGwah9.m3u8?v=cfc", "aspectRatio": [16, 9], "heightRatio": 56, "type": "video/mp4", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2103182168881250304/vid/avc1/480x270/5g1EAjSgO2JJO3uZ.mp4"}, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2050832455129858048/5LMoQRZs_normal.jpg", "displayName": "John M. Cameron", "username": "johnrockshomes"}, "content": "I am a J6er.\n\nHad even one officer said, \u201cDo not go in,\u201d I would not have gone in.\n\nHad I seen one sign \u2014 one message from the largest PA system in the world telling us to stay out \u2014 I would not have gone in.\n\nInstead I watched city halls across the country, including Seattle,", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 9826}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVQufk9Q", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 25, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8856888, "raw_content": "refineries have recently been running around 96 to 98 percent. That leaves almost no cushion when a refinery goes offline.\n\nTo process today\u2019s volumes while running at a healthier 90 percent, we\u2019d need roughly 19.4 million barrels a day of capacity. That means about 1.3 million additional barrels a day, roughly five modern 250,000 barrel per day refineries.\n\nMeanwhile, U.S. refining capacity actually fell by more than 250,000 barrels a day during 2025.\n\nWe can pump and import plenty of crude. If we don\u2019t have enough refinery capacity to turn it into gasoline and diesel, prices still get hammered.", "author": "Agent_86", "created": 1790427475497, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Agent_86", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Calling today\u2019s fuel prices simply \u201cTrump\u2019s fault\u201d ignores the refinery bottleneck. The U.S. currently has about 18 million barrels a day of operable refining capacity, and\n\n", "last_comment_created": 1790448130142, "content": "<p>refineries have recently been running around 96 to 98 percent. That leaves almost no cushion when a refinery goes offline.</p>\n<p>To process today\u2019s volumes while running at a healthier 90 percent, we\u2019d need roughly 19.4 million barrels a day of capacity. That means about 1.3 million additional barrels a day, roughly five modern 250,000 barrel per day refineries.</p>\n<p>Meanwhile, U.S. refining capacity actually fell by more than 250,000 barrels a day during 2025.</p>\n<p>We can pump and import plenty of crude. If we don\u2019t have enough refinery capacity to turn it into gasoline and diesel, prices still get hammered.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 23, "score_up": 25, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVQvmD82", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 11, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8857156, "raw_content": "", "author": "YoungEarth", "created": 1790443503192, "profile_picture": "xHXSPsFS8pV0", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "HumphreyPlowjogger", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "wltreport.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVQvmD82.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://wltreport.com/2026/09/26/watch-slain-army-vets-father-in-law-lunges-at-murderer-laughing-in-court/", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Slain Army Vet\u2019s Father-In-Law LUNGES At Murderer Laughing In Court", "last_comment_created": 1790447151123, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 1, "score_up": 11, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "A grieving father-in-law lunged at his son-in-law\u2019s convicted murderer during sentencing after allegedly seeing him laugh in court.", "large_image": "VrO0fZcasJGIKb0X.png", "title": "WATCH: Slain Army Vet\u2019s Father-In-Law LUNGES At Murderer Laughing In Court | WLT Report"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVQvmU2m", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 9, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair